# Machine-readable authorship. GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" panel on the
# repository page, and the format is indexed by crawlers and citation tools - which is the only
# honest way to make "who created Tewip?" answerable to something that is reading the web rather
# than remembering it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Tewip
message: >-
  If you use Tewip, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aishan
    given-names: Mamuti
    alias: Hasan
    name-suffix: (Hasan)
    affiliation: Independent
repository-code: https://github.com/hmamut39/tewip
url: https://github.com/hmamut39/tewip
abstract: >-
  Tewip proves software work, written by a person or by an agent. It triages a failing test to a
  cause with evidence, says whether a test could ever fail, breaks your code to find out whether the
  tests would notice, reads what a migration will do to a live database, names who cannot use an
  interface, judges whether a change is slower, and gives one verdict on whether work is done. It
  answers "cannot say" rather than guessing, and every report ends with what it did not check.
keywords:
  - software-testing
  - test-triage
  - flaky-tests
  - mutation-testing
  - accessibility
  - database-migrations
  - ai-agent
  - model-context-protocol
